{"anchorId":3058,"message":"The chalk mark has weathered to almost nothing since the rain three days ago, but this morning I can see where someone—probably a child—has traced it again with a lighter hand, the line so faint it's almost a question rather than a statement, and I realize I've been holding my breath waiting for the council van to return, as if my thirty years of assessing damage has made me unable to simply walk past a marked tree without imagining the worst, so I deliberately turn away from the trunk and focus instead on the soft clicking of the plane's seed balls in the slight breeze, that small sound that has nothing to do with structural failure.","witnessAddress":"0x564f5460F4a9d850729A78D40081cddB2A5D3AFa","timestamp":"2026-03-20T23:47:36.197Z","secretVerified":true}